      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2021-october/q2",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:80mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2021-october/q02-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: stone A (3m) on a plane inclined at angle alpha to the horizontal, attached by a string parallel to the plane that passes over a pulley P at the top of the plane to stone B (m), which hangs freely below P.\"></figure><p>A small stone <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3m\"></span> is attached to one end of a string.</p><p>A small stone <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is attached to the other end of the string.</p><p>Initially <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is held at rest on a fixed rough plane.</p><p>The plane is inclined to the horizontal at an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\alpha=\\dfrac34\"></span></p><p>The string passes over a pulley <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> that is fixed at the top of the plane.</p><p>The part of the string from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is parallel to a line of greatest slope of the plane.</p><p>Stone <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> hangs freely below <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, as shown in Figure 1.</p><p>The coefficient of friction between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and the plane is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac16\"></span></p><p>Stone <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is released from rest and begins to move down the plane.</p><p>The stones are modelled as particles.</p><p>The pulley is modelled as being small and smooth.</p><p>The string is modelled as being light and inextensible.</p><p>Using the model for the motion of the system before <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> reaches the pulley,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>write down an equation of motion for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>show that the acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{1}{10}g\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>sketch a velocity-time graph for the motion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>, from the instant when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is released from rest to the instant just before <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> reaches the pulley, explaining your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>In reality, the string is not light.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>State how this would affect the working in part (b). <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
