      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2021-october/q3",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:55mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2021-october/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: a beam AB of length 2a with A on horizontal ground and B against a vertical wall, inclined at angle theta to the ground.\"></figure><p>A beam <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> has mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2a\"></span>.</p><p>The beam rests in equilibrium with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> on rough horizontal ground and with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> against a smooth vertical wall.</p><p>The beam is inclined to the horizontal at an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span>, as shown in Figure 2.</p><p>The coefficient of friction between the beam and the ground is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span></p><p>The beam is modelled as a uniform rod resting in a vertical plane that is perpendicular to the wall.</p><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\\geqslant\\dfrac12\\cot\\theta\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>A horizontal force of magnitude <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kmg\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant, is now applied to the beam at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><p>This force acts in a direction that is perpendicular to the wall and towards the wall.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac54\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu=\\dfrac12\"></span> and the beam is now in limiting equilibrium,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>use the model to find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
