      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:80mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2021-october/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: a stone projected from O at the top of a vertical cliff with speed 65 m s^-1 at angle alpha above the horizontal; O is 70 m vertically above N on horizontal ground, and the path lands at A.\"></figure><p>A small stone is projected with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"65\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> at the top of a vertical cliff.</p><p>Point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"70\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> vertically above the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span>.</p><p>Point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span> is on horizontal ground.</p><p>The stone is projected at an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> above the horizontal, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\alpha=\\dfrac{5}{12}\"></span></p><p>The stone hits the ground at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, as shown in Figure 3.</p><p>The stone is modelled as a particle moving freely under gravity.</p><p><strong>The acceleration due to gravity is modelled as having magnitude <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\"></span></strong></p><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find the time taken for the stone to travel from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>find the speed of the stone at the instant just before it hits the ground at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>One limitation of the model is that it ignores air resistance.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>State one other limitation of the model that could affect the reliability of your answers. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
